Hooks for thermal-guard
=======================

Executables placed here run as root when the matching action fires. They are
files rather than configuration options on purpose: the LuCI page may edit
every option in /etc/config/thermal-guard, but it cannot write into this
directory, so nothing changed through the web interface can introduce code
that runs as root.

Put a hook here over SSH and make it executable (chmod 0755). A hook that is
missing or not executable is skipped, and the daemon logs that the action could
not be carried out.

  notify        Receives the message text on stdin. Only needed for a delivery
                that notify_url cannot express, a local mailer for example.
                When notify_url is set as well, it is tried first and this hook
                is the fallback.

  stage1        Runs when stage 2 of 3 starts and stage1_action is 'command'.
  stage2        Runs when stage 3 of 3 starts and stage2_action is 'command'.

  modem-temp    Runs when modem_source is 'command'. Has to print the modem
                temperature in whole degrees Celsius on stdout, nothing else.

Keep them short and make them return promptly. The daemon waits for a hook
before it continues its cycle, and a hook that hangs delays the next reading.

Example, a notify hook for a local mailer:

  #!/bin/sh
  exec mail -s "thermal-guard" root
